  "testbench": {
    "name": "comparator-offset-transient-mc",
    "description": "Transient Monte-Carlo input-referred offset of the WHOLE latch (strobe -> decision) -- comparator_dut, the actual DR-0001 regenerative topology, not the loop-broken comparator_dut_analog reduced sub-model comparator-offset-mc measures.",
    "claim": "sim/dut.json binds design/comparator.spice (id comparator-dr0001, provenance schematic), the ratified topology from spec/decision-records/0001-comparator-topology.md ('DR-0001'). This record substantiates that a transient Monte-Carlo digital-staircase offset sweep genuinely runs and genuinely detects SG13G2's per-instance local mismatch across the WHOLE latch (comparator_dut: input pair, tail, cross-coupled regenerative pair, reset devices, isolation inverters, SR output latch) -- STILL NOT evidence toward README.md#target-specification's Offset-sigma row on its own: that ratification is a separate, later act (spec/porting-plan.md's third step in this chain). Unlike comparator-offset-mc, this bench excludes NOTHING from the topology by construction: it is not a lower bound.",
    "experiment": "comparator-offset-transient-mc",
    "directory": "testbench",
    "netlist": "tb_offset_transient_mc.spice",
    "netlist_sha256": "00a9c7ccc9798e023bb2a5c4ab891ed65964cf4d6c105b9b7a6141cc0b77fd6d",
    "manifest_sha256": "3254e6566b92805626dce6b844aad83e89e0f882e21ddad7117de03a746e259b",
    "nominal_supply_v": 1.2,
    "supply_tolerance": 0.1
  },
  "checks": {
    "n_out_of_range": {
      "max": 0.0,
      "description": "RANGE-ADEQUACY GATE. lowcount (the number of the 33 staircase levels that read LOW) must land strictly between 0 and 33 for every draw, i.e. the true per-draw offset must fall inside the swept -48..+48 mV window. A draw that pins to one end means that draw's offset landed outside the window and vos/sig_vos_mv for that draw is meaningless (clamped, not measured) -- this check must read exactly 0 for the record to be trustworthy. If a real corner ever needs it, the window (DV_MIN/DV_STEP/N_LEVELS in the deck) widens, not this floor."
    },
    "sig_vos_mv": {
      "min": 0.05,
      "description": "MISMATCH-ON GUARD, mirroring comparator-offset-mc's identical check. --sabotage-corners forces every corner to plain mos_tt (mismatch off, sim/harness/corners.py), which must and does collapse this measurement toward exactly zero. 0.05 mV is far below anything a real sub-micron latch can achieve, so this floor only catches a collapsed (mismatch-free) population, not a design assertion. sqrt(abs(...)) guards the same negative-variance-from-floating-point-noise trap comparator-offset-mc's tb.json documents for the mismatch-off case."
    },
    "mean_vos_sem": {
      "min": -5.0,
      "max": 5.0,
      "description": "SYMMETRY CHECK, expressed in standard errors of the RAW (uncorrected) sigma so it is independent of the quantization-correction term. The population mean offset must be ~0 because the circuit is nominally symmetric; +/-5 standard errors is a ~6e-7 two-sided false-alarm rate at this N. A mean outside it means a systematic asymmetry (a netlist error, a genuinely asymmetric topology, or a level-list off-center of true zero)."
    },
    "vbias_anchor_mv": {
      "min": 50.0,
      "max": 1200.0,
      "description": "CORNER-SENSITIVITY SANITY FLOOR. The bias pin's own voltage is a V_th proxy and strongly corner/temperature dependent, the same contract node (ibias) comparator-offset-mc anchors on. A floor-only sanity range (not per-axis-calibrated here, unlike comparator-offset-mc's own vbias_anchor_mv floors, since this bench's first committed record is this experiment's own calibration point -- see README.md 'Calibration' for why a per-axis floor was deliberately deferred rather than guessed)."
    }
  },
